纯产物在过程中损失了。

133
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:36,560
There is one more thing to keep in mind.
还有一件事需要记住。

134
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:41,520
Sometimes your crystals will refuse to grow, even if you use an ice bath to cool them down
有时候你的晶体就是不肯长出来，即使你用冰浴把它们冷却

135
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:43,160
to a lower temperature.
到更低的温度也不行。

136
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:47,920
This can be caused by the glass surface in the beaker being too smooth.
这可能是因为烧杯的玻璃表面太光滑了。

137
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:53,860
One solution is to use a glass rod to scrape your beaker on the bottom and sides.
一个解决办法是用玻璃棒刮擦烧杯的底部和侧壁。

138
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:59,280
This will generate some loose glass particles upon which your crystals can grow.
这会产生一些松散的玻璃颗粒，晶体可以在上面生长。

139
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:04,240
Another good method to initiate crystallization is to add a few crystals of your pure product
另一个引发结晶的好方法是，往溶液中加入几粒纯产物的晶体，

140
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:09,200
to the solution so that other molecules can join an existing lattice.
这样其他分子就可以加入已有的晶格。

141
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:12,240
This is called using a seed crystal.
这叫做使用晶种。

142
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:17,640
In some more advanced recrystallizations, we may need to use multisolvent systems.
在一些更高级的重结晶中，我们可能需要使用混合溶剂体系。

143
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:22,240
In this case, this first solvent dissolves the impure product, while the addition of
这种情况下，第一种溶剂溶解不纯的产物，而加入

144
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:26,900
a second solvent causes the pure product to gradually crystallize.
第二种溶剂会使纯产物逐渐结晶出来。

145
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:30,520
But as that's a bit more advanced, this will be all for recrystallization.
不过这部分稍微高级一些，所以关于重结晶就讲到这里。

146
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:32,920
Let's move on to some other techniques.
让我们继续学习其他一些技术。
